invariant: INV-13
file: srv_out.c
catches: srv_tcp_nonblocking_test
reason: a record the server's transport refused keeps the handler's
  default alert, decode_error, which says the peer sent a malformed
  message, where RFC 9846 section 6.2 names internal_error for this
  side's own failure. bin/srv_tcp_nonblocking_test refuses the
  ServerHello's record and requires internal_error from the failed
  session.

--- old
    int rc = emit(h->t, p, n);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        h->alert = ALERT_INTERNAL_ERROR;
    }
--- new
    int rc = emit(h->t, p, n);
